---
id: soy-ginger-sesame-shrimp
title: Soy-Ginger-Sesame Shrimp (Poke Style)
category: modular_protein

yield:
  servings: 1
  cooked_g: 300

storage:
  fridge_days: 2
  freezer_friendly: false

---

Thaw: tip the whole bag of @cooked-pacific-white-shrimp{1%package} into a bowl of cold tap water with 1 tsp of salt. Let sit for ~thaw-time{10%min} (7 to 10 minutes) until completely thawed, then pinch the tails off.

Dry: spread the shrimp on 2 to 3 sheets of paper towel and press dry. Wet shrimp dilute the marinade and it won't stick.

Mix: in your meal bowl, stir together 1.5 tbsp of @soy-sauce-less-sodium{1.5%tbsp}, 1 tsp of @sesame-oil{1%tsp}, 1 tsp of @rice-vinegar{1%tsp}, @garlic-powder{1/4%tsp}, and @ground-ginger{1/4%tsp}. Add the dried shrimp and stir to coat.

Rest: let sit for ~rest-time{5%min} at room temperature while you plate your carb or side.

Serve: spoon the shrimp over a warm base (rice or buckwheat) and pour the liquid left in the bowl over the top.
